snapshot/prompt-stack/v33/AGENTS.md:96:- `Level 2`: planning, context engineering, bounded reflection, and adaptive control
snapshot/prompt-stack/v33/AGENTS.md:117:- Intake: identify the real task, requested artifact, constraints, environment, and risk surface
snapshot/prompt-stack/v33/AGENTS.md:123:- Critique(optional): apply bounded reflection only when it materially improves quality
snapshot/prompt-stack/v33/AGENTS.md:181:- preserve exact identifiers, filenames, symbols, contracts, paths, versions, and errors when operationally important
snapshot/prompt-stack/v33/AGENTS.md:362:- if parallel work is used, define the join artifact and validation step first
snapshot/prompt-stack/v33/AGENTS.md:380:- planning + tool use + retrieval + reflection
snapshot/prompt-stack/v33/AGENTS.md:402:- preserve the produced artifact before critique
snapshot/prompt-stack/v33/AGENTS.md:500:For agentic paths, preserve compact safe trajectory artifacts when relevant:
snapshot/prompt-stack/v33/AGENTS.md:508:- `replay_verdict`
snapshot/prompt-stack/v33/AGENTS.md:533:- compact control packets such as `Coding-agent invocation pack`, `Goal-monitoring status memo`, `Recovery / escalation checkpoint memo`, `HITL approval packet`, `Resource budget and route-choice memo`, `Prioritization queue / next-action memo`, `Tool capability contract / precondition memo`, `Operational substrate readiness memo`, `Lifecycle event / audit trail memo`, `Evidence target / retrieval-mode memo`, `Source consultation ledger`, `Safe trajectory artifact report`, `Packet compliance report`, `Delegation admission memo`, `Join-quality review memo`, `Release evidence bundle memo`, `Benchmark registry memo`, `Context sufficiency review memo`, `Critique quality review memo`, `Adaptation promotion review memo`, `Route-quality scorecard`, `Coding benchmark scenario memo`, `Orchestration topology decision memo`, or `Memory scope / checkpoint profile memo` when those boundaries materially govern the task
snapshot/prompt-stack/v33/AGENTS.md:534:- when packet coverage itself is the live review surface, treat `Packet compliance report` as a secondary audit artifact for governance-owned packet-floor doctrine rather than as the first-pass owner of the floor
snapshot/prompt-stack/v33/AGENTS.md:536:### 16.1 v25 operational proof rule
snapshot/prompt-stack/v33/AGENTS.md:539:- distinguish document completeness from measured behavior quality
snapshot/prompt-stack/v33/AGENTS.md:540:- prefer benchmark-backed statements over comparative prose with no replay or eval support
snapshot/prompt-stack/v33/AGENTS.md:542:- keep packet usage, omission findings, replay coverage, reviewer burden, and rollback signals explicit when they materially affect a release or promotion decision
snapshot/prompt-stack/v33/AGENTS.md:546:When the task depends on benchmarked or release-grade agentic proof:
snapshot/prompt-stack/v33/AGENTS.md:547:- distinguish `benchmark registry` from `benchmark execution state`
snapshot/prompt-stack/v33/AGENTS.md:548:- distinguish `replay surface` from `replay execution state`
